{"items":[{"recordId":"teach-n0000808","units":[{"role":"statement","basis":"source","text":"The paper claims that the systems under discussion have Church–Rosser confluence.","requires":[],"citationRequired":true},{"role":"statement","basis":"source","text":"The paper also claims that these systems are optimal according to the relevant notion of optimality.","requires":[],"citationRequired":true}]},{"recordId":"teach-n0000809","units":[{"role":"definition","basis":"source","text":"Church–Rosser confluence means that when a system has multiple divergent paths from the same starting point, those paths can each be continued until they reach a common result.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false},{"role":"intuition","basis":"source","text":"Thus, different intermediate choices do not prevent the system from eventually agreeing on the same outcome.","requires":[],"citationRequired":false}]}]}
